... never having dealt with AlphaPC's (and not knowing anything about
them), I'm wondering whether these things are capable of running
Tru64/Digital UNIX. What I hear from /some/ are "AlphaPC's are not
capable of running Tru64 because of its firmware/BIOS"; another group
tells me "yes, it is capable of running Tru64 UNIX". No one has been
able to give me much specifics on why or why not, other than the fact
that the firmware on the AlphaPC motherboards don't have SRM (??). At
the same rate, no one that I've spoken to cared enough to even put
"AlphaPC" issuses in their consideration queue. Now I'm left wondering
whether the AlphaPC motherboard's firmware chip is /capable/ of holding
SRM, or only ARC (do they even use ARC?).

If the problem is simply obtaining SRM, it wouldn't be a problem -- but
if there are limitations on what can be flashed, <blah> being
incompatible, etc. on the AlphaPC motherboards, I guess that's a whole
new set of problems.

Any new light on this issue would be appreciated.

