Tru64 runs fine on AlphaPC.  Just did an install over the holidays.
It only has room for either ARC or for SRM.  The Tru64 distribution
comes with a firmware CD you can use to update SRM.  Or you can go
to ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v5.1/alphapc164lx/
(that URL is for the LX) and create a floppy to load SRM.

Now, that said, there are restrictions on hardware support.  Not
every PCI card will work.  In general, DEC ethernet cards-DE500
(and those that use the DECchip, (21140, etc)), VGA S3 Trio64, and
if you want SCSI - Qlogic such as QLA1040.  The full list is much
larger and is in the SPD (the boards supported are also there) 
see http://www.digital.com/info/SP7070/

Ray T.



