> Should I understand this as filtering _only_ works when defining a
> remote printer as a TCP/IP printer with portnumber ?

Yes that is correct, filtering is available for every connection method
except lpd remote.

> In your example you use both a if and a of filter... I've seen this in
> examples too, but I'm not sure I understand why... can you explain why I
> need to define a filter both as if and of ?

The output filter processes the lpd generated text banner page. The
input filter processes the file and provides accounting.  When a job
contains multiple files an input filter is started for each file.

Lpd inserts special characters in the banner page that must be detected by
the output filter. I recommend using an OS provided filter for the output
filter.

> I use the af part to tell the script what printer (stuff before the dot)
> to print to when the data is filtered, and what kind of printer (stuff
> after the dot) it is, so the filter (/usr/local/bin/printfilter.sh) know
> what to do.
> The printfilter is a custom written script that does alot of stuff to
> the data running thru.

Instead of using the accounting file argument to pass additional
information add it after the filter specification using filter specific
switches. In the printcap example I used -a and -b.

The new tcp/ip queue should look similar to:

vojens1|VOJENS1:\
        :ct=tcp:\
        :if=/usr/local/bin/printfilter.sh -avojens1_filtreret -bdde1070:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lpd/vojens1.err:\
        :lp=@vojens1/dde_nct2_2070:\
        :mx#0:\
        :of=/usr/lbin/lpf:\
        :pl#66:\
        :pw#80:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd/vojens1:\
        :sh:\
        :xf=/usr/lbin/xf:

The XF setting specifies the filter to process the lpr -x switch. By default
this is set to the xf (transparent or pass-thru) filter script.

OF has been configured to use the lpf print filter. I'm sure there is a better

choice but I don't know your OS version or printer make/model. Suggestions:

pcl printer             :of=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Chpdj680c.pcf:\
text printer            :of=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Cgeneric_text.pcf:\
PostScript printer      :of=/usr/lbin/ln03rof:\


--------------------
