Sylviane Molinet wrote:

> I have problems to mount cdrom for users, only root can do that
> Any suggestions are welcome
> Sylviane

You can try changing device attributes on the device driver

chmod a+rw /dev/rzNc where N is your CD-ROM

You can check which one it is by looking at the startup log
uerf -c oper | more

or by looking at the files in /dev

file /dev/rz?c

CD-ROM will be RRD-XXXX device.

Hope this helps,

Pedro.






