Sylviane Molinet wrote:
> I have problems to mount cdrom for users, only root can do that
> Any suggestions are welcome

... and that's how it *should* be. Why do you need users mounting
devices? For example, someone could easily make a CD with a binary with
a setuid bit, owned by root, and obtain root access to the system.

If you want local users with console access to be able to mount a
CD-ROM, though, you could write a small wrapper to check the UID of that
user (to see if it matches a local user) and do a setuid() to 0, mount
the CD-ROM (but with options such as 'nodev', 'nosuid', etc), and exit.
Same deal with umount, so they can take the CD-ROM out.

